KZ2 6085: the frame thread's sleep between drain passes ends when the title has written more commands
(KZ2_WALKER_POLL_US=<n>, off by default; ENHANCEMENT, not bit-exact: it changes when labels and flips reach the
title, not what is drawn).
A drain pass walks up to the put it read at its start, and the sleep after it (cellGcm_walker_wait(4) in port/kz2
main.cpp's frame_clock) is a flat Sleep unless a park (6038) or an acquire wait (6082) is armed. Commands the title
writes during or just after a pass therefore wait for the sleep to end, on the thread the frame waits for.
Measured on 0.1.13 (native Windows, Ryzen 9 9950X3D, RTX 4090; an unattended run of Corinth Sands, the player standing
in the fight): KZ3_PROF on rsx:frame with KZ2_PROF_STACK=1, 30.5k samples: 26.6 % under cellGcm_walker_wait (15.4 %
in the event wait, 11.2 % in the plain Sleep). A/B, three rounds in rotated order, 120 s runs, the level's average
frame rate: off 42.73 +- 0.48, KZ2_WALKER_POLL_US=0 44.83 +- 0.68 (+4.9 %, +0.4 cores), =250 44.63 +- 0.61 (+4.5 %,
+0.14 cores); every run with the switch above every run without (issue #102).
The change: the drain records the put it starts from (s_wp_seen_put). With the switch, the wait runs in <n> us slices
(a high-resolution waitable timer together with the wake event; 0 = yield-spin, capped at 4000) and returns 2 when the
control register's put differs from the recorded one, or, while patch 7014's park watch is on, the armed park word
differs from s_park_watch_w (whoever wrote it). 7014's arm stores that word only with the watch on: with
KZ2_PARK_WATCH=0 the park test is skipped and the put test alone ends a slice (else the stale word never matches and
the frame thread would run drain, pump and wait back to back). 6082's acquire label is checked each slice as well.
cellGcm_walker_poll_counts gives the two counts. If the high-resolution timer cannot be made, the slices are
yield-spins and a one-time [walker-poll] line says so.
Not checked: Proton, a CPU with few cores (a yield-spin there may cost more than it gives), input latency.
Host test: tools/runtime/test_walker_wait_poll.sh (wiring, and the decision rule with negative controls, the park
watch on and off).
Upstream candidate (ps3recomp libs/video/cellGcmSys.c; needs the frame thread's sleep to go through one function).

